You're right. The same word is in Croatian "neka" ("Neka se djeca igraju")
and in English "Let". The sentence you gave ("Let the children play") is
direct English translation due to the fact that grammar concerning 3rd
person imperatives is same. Perhaps it is because you are native English
speaker that you did not recognise this in your language and turned to
Russian to explore it, perhaps not... :) Here, "let" does not mean "allow",
I believe.

Ambiguity. Universally guilty.
